---
layout: changelog
title: Cached list queries use up to 69% less memory
date: 2026-09-25
cover: /images/blog/faster-list-caching-binary-format/cover.avif
---

Appwrite now stores its Redis cache in igbinary, a compact binary format, instead of JSON. The change covers list queries cached with a `ttl` and the data Appwrite caches on most requests, such as sessions, API keys, and table schemas.

In benchmarks, a cached page of 1,000 rows or more took 67% to 69% less memory, and one server handled up to 29% more cached `listRows` requests per second. The change is live on Appwrite Cloud and ships in self-hosted Appwrite 2.3. Self-hosted instances need no migration, because Appwrite reads an old JSON entry as a cache miss and writes it again in the new format.

